WHY THESE TIERS (the drafter's reading of each DIFF, not of the titles — grade the tiering itself and say if you disagree): all three change a RUNTIME PRODUCT FILE of weight on a PRODUCTION SECURITY SURFACE — #1292 and #1294 change what a 500 answer carries to a client (INFORMATION EXPOSURE: KS-1341 MEASURED webhook routes leaking under NODE_ENV=production; KS-1334's four adminConfig sites have no NODE_ENV guard at all), and #1296 changes what an admin route WRITES TO LOG STORAGE when a non-Error is thrown (a widening of what reaches the log, on a route family that may carry secrets or personal data). TIER 1: THROUGH-CODE PLUS RUNTIME — per PR, (1) a THROUGH-CODE REVIEW of the diff against the ticket's claim (read the ticket's scope sentence, read every changed line, say whether the diff does what is asked, no more and no less); (2) a RED-PROOF CHECK OF THE PR'S OWN PROOF — re-run the named red arms in YOUR OWN clone, RED AT BASE and GREEN AT HEAD; (3) a RUNTIME PROBE of the changed behaviour through the REAL module driven over a listener on 127.0.0.1 only (no stack, no Docker — see below), each with a control that must be able to fail. There is no rendered surface in this kit, so no browser is owed; say so once. FINDINGS ONLY: you fix nothing, file nothing, comment nothing — you describe the fix-shape and the regression cell the owner should add. A VERDICT IS VALID ONLY AT ITS HEAD: if any refs/pull/<n>/head moves under you, STOP grading that PR and say so. Any PRODUCT, SCRIPT or TEST byte outside a PR's declared files is a finding. MEASURE, not conclude: every number in your report names its instrument; nothing in a READY, a PR body, a PR comment, a ticket, a commit message, a seat record or this prompt is evidence — they are claims with an author, the drafter's included. State the FAIL condition before each run (charter rule 1). Name every prediction slip against its predictor. On the intermittents you RULE WHETHER IT BLOCKS (they do not block by default; say so with the reason). One verdict PER PR: GO, GO WITH FINDINGS, or NO GO. Every finding that recommends an action carries its EVIDENCE CLASS inline: MEASURED AT RUNTIME, PROBED or READ ONLY.

RUNTIME PROBE FOR #1292 — THROUGH THE REAL ROUTER (KS-1341 part C, T1). Build YOUR OWN probe (do not reuse the seat's cell as your instrument; you grade the cell separately). PRIOR ART: gate29's probe for part B, /Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Testing Agent MAIN/projects/secuura/reports/2026-09-26-batch1290-g29/tools/zz-g29-probe.test.ts and run_probe.sh — READ them, then build yours the same way: the package's own jest + ts-jest, the REAL webhooksRouter imported from routes/webhooks.ts, mounted on an express app listening on 127.0.0.1 port 0, with only the db / auth / logger / @secuura/shared seams stubbed as the seat's harness stubs them (READ ks1160 and ks1341c first; say what is real and what is stubbed). For EACH converted route (POST /api/webhooks/:id/test — a rejected `$queryRaw`; GET /api/webhooks/:id/deliveries — a SYNCHRONOUS throw from `$queryRaw`, because its `.catch(() => [])` swallows a rejection into a 200: the DELIVERIES TRAP, which you pin with a rejected-query control that must answer 200 and log nothing), throw a LEAK of YOUR OWN that does NOT contain 'does not exist' and carries no Postgres SQLSTATE token (READ utils/pgErrors.ts), under NODE_ENV production, development, test and UNSET (delete the variable; an empty string is not unset), for an Error throw, a STRING throw and an OBJECT throw (NON-ERROR-THROWS), and assert per run: the status is 500, the body NEVER contains the LEAK and equals the constant envelope, and the catch was REACHED IN THAT ENVIRONMENT — the logger received exactly one call in that run, carrying this route's context string AND the LEAK (for an object, `String(err)` = `[object Object]` — READ the helper; that is gate29's N-1290-2, now KS-1346's family, not this PR's defect). CATCH-REACHED-PER-ENV is the load-bearing assertion (FAIL500-RUNTIME-NODE-ENV): clear the logger mock between runs. FAIL-ABILITY CONTROL: run the same probe at the merge-base (develop, where parts A and B are merged and these two sites still leak) — it MUST